 When a check fails: read the last lines of its output first; they name the file and line. For a test, run it alone (`python -m pytest -q tests/test_name.py::test_name`). A test that did not run is not a pass: to see why tests were skipped, run `python -m pytest -q -rs`, which prints one line per skip reason (for example "could not import 'playwright.sync_api'", "node is not installed", "no gitleaks program on PATH"). To make a missing secret scan a failure instead of a skip, set `DPLD_REQUIRE_SCAN=1` and `GITLEAKS_BIN` to the program's path.
 
+What the two secret checks reported, measured on 2026-11-13 with gitleaks 8.30.1 and this repository's `.gitleaks.toml`. The test values were made up and put after the prefix `hadavin-dx_` in a `key=value` line, in files named `cfg.txt`, `notes.properties` and `x_api_key.txt`. Gitleaks (rule `generic-api-key`) reported values of 20, 30, 40, 50 and 60 random lowercase letters and digits. It did not report values of letters only, of words joined by hyphens, or of one repeated letter, at any of those lengths. One digit added to the hyphenated words made gitleaks report them; one digit added to the repeated letter did not. So the cause looks like "no digit" or "too little variety" in the value, not the prefix; the rule inside gitleaks was not read. The real project key holds a digit and was reported once its allowlist was removed. A prefix inside a line of ordinary text was not reported by gitleaks at any length.
+
+The repository scan (`patterns.txt`, pattern 9, `[A-Za-z0-9+/=_-]{40,}`) reports an unbroken run of 40 or more of those characters. The prefix and a key name before `=` count towards the 40; a dot, a space or a quote ends the run. It reported every `key=value` line above, so a letters-only second project key in `sonar-project.properties` is seen by that scan alone. The exception for the real key (last line of `exceptions.txt`, the `sonar.projectKey` allowlist in `.gitleaks.toml`) therefore has to stay exact. `tests/test_gitleaks_exceptions.py` plants near-misses in a temporary copy and fails if either exception is widened. To add a second key of this shape, add its exact text, never a wider pattern or a whole file, and keep that test passing. `.gitattributes` forces LF endings; the real line with CRLF endings is reported by gitleaks, not by the repository scan.
+
 ## What each promise rests on
 
 The desk was stopped on purpose at each of ten crash points and restarted; nine of them are simulated by an exception raised inside the program, and only D2 is a real process kill (`docs/limits.md`). The table says what had happened at each point and what the result was. "Keyed" and "blind" are explained in the README under "Words used here". The two columns are the kind of MAIL system. The outcome at C0 and C1 depends on the kind of CRM instead (both mail kinds gave the same result in the tests, `tests/test_flow.py`, `EXPECT_MORE`), so those two rows say so in words.
